+        F7 (pf-adversary, this round): the test this replaces called
+        ``_session`` twice with two DIFFERENT tokens and called the second
+        one ``relogged`` -- ``_synthetic_client_login_pc``/``ensure_account``
+        key the account by the token string, and ``_V25_REAL_CREATE_PC``
+        mints a character every time it runs, so two tokens is two accounts
+        and two characters, never a relog.  The world's grave book is
+        process-global (``PANYA 20260906_1057/1140``: a scene's deaths
+        belong to the world, not the connection), so a fresh SECOND
+        identity would see the first one's kill too -- the test that named
+        itself a relogin was proving the SAME thing
+        ``test_a_second_session_in_the_same_scene_sees_the_first_ones_kill``
+        already proves, under a different name.
+
+        A real relog is the SAME token (so ``ensure_account`` resolves the
+        SAME account_id) without ``_V25_REAL_CREATE_PC`` (which would mint a
+        SECOND character on that account instead of re-entering the first
+        one): login, then ``list_characters`` finds the character the
+        earlier ``_session(token)`` call already created, and start_game
+        selects it directly.
